    {
      "qid": "6575994585c3d03a580b61f7",
      "n": 4,
      "type": "mcq",
      "concept": "Syllogism",
      "confidence": "high",
      "marks_pos": 1.0,
      "marks_neg": 0.25,
      "question": "Two statements are given, followed by two conclusions numbered I and II. Assuming the statements to be true, even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts, decide which of the conclusions logically follow(s) from the statements.\n\n**Statements:**\n\nAll surveys are research.\n\nSome surveys are books.\n\n**Conclusions:**\n\nI. Some research are surveys.\n\nII. All books are research.",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "1",
          "text": "Only Conclusion II follows."
        },
        {
          "label": "2",
          "text": "Only Conclusion I follows."
        },
        {
          "label": "3",
          "text": "Both Conclusions I and II follow."
        },
        {
          "label": "4",
          "text": "Neither Conclusion I nor II follows."
        }
      ],
      "correct": "2",
      "solution": "Given Statements:\n\nAll surveys are research.\n\nSome surveys are books.\n\nThe least possible Venn diagram is as follows:\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/842d71ba47305311724e2b4a805b63af953b249097a4c4162223b4fe0445b707.png] \n\nConclusions:\n\nI. Some research are surveys. - **True** (because All surveys are research given. So, Some research are surveys it is definite)\n\nII. All books are research. - **False** (because Some surveys are books and All surveys are research. So, it is possible but not definite)\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"Only Conclusion I follows\".**",
      "solution_images": [
        {
          "url": "https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/842d71ba47305311724e2b4a805b63af953b249097a4c4162223b4fe0445b707.png",
