    {
      "qid": "65759a394bff7c6831d0a87f",
      "n": 9,
      "type": "mcq",
      "concept": "Puzzle",
      "confidence": "high",
      "marks_pos": 1.0,
      "marks_neg": 0.25,
      "question": "Which two signs should be interchanged to make the given equation correct?\n\n264 ÷ 4 × 7 = 87 − 370 + 5",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "1",
          "text": "= and −"
        },
        {
          "label": "2",
          "text": "= and ×"
        },
        {
          "label": "3",
          "text": "= and +"
        },
        {
          "label": "4",
          "text": "= and ÷"
        }
      ],
      "correct": "1",
      "solution": "[IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/9f1f11fbb4e091305a6b414e74c3aec25b8d519670a1f3bd65f5bd4eb1bdcd68.png] \n\nGiven equation: 264 ÷ 4 × 7 = 87 − 370 + 5\n\n**Option 1) = and -**\n\nTwo signs need to be interchanged then:\n\n⇒ __**264 ÷ 4**__ × 7 - 87 = 370 + 5\n\n⇒__** 66 × 7**__ - 87 = 370 + 5\n\n⇒ __**462 - 87**__ = __**370 + 5**__\n\n**⇒ 375 = 375**\n\nOption 2) = and ×\n\nTwo signs need to be interchanged then:\n\n⇒ __**264 ÷ 4**__ = __**7 × 87**__ − 370 + 5\n\n⇒ 66 = __**609**__ − 370 __**+ 5**__\n\n⇒ 66 = __**614 − 370**__\n\n⇒ 66 ≠ 244\n\nOption 3) = and +\n\nTwo signs need to be interchanged then:\n\n⇒ __**264 ÷ 4**__ × 7 + 87 − 370 = 5\n\n⇒ __**66 × 7**__ + 87 − 370 = 5\n\n⇒ __462____** + 87**__ − 370 = 5\n\n⇒ **__529__**__** − 370**__ = 5\n\n⇒ 179 ≠ 5\n\nOption 4) = and ÷\n\nTwo signs need to be interchanged then:\n\n⇒ 264 = __**4 × 7 ÷ 87**__ − 370 + 5\n\n⇒ 264 = __**0.32**__ − 370 __**+ 5**__\n\n⇒ 264 = __**5.32 − 370**__\n\n⇒ 264 ≠ -364.68\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"= and -\".**",
      "solution_images": [
        {
          "url": "https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/9f1f11fbb4e091305a6b414e74c3aec25b8d519670a1f3bd65f5bd4eb1bdcd68.png",
          "alt": ""
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "Logical Puzzle"
      ]
    },
